# Testing

- Pure logic (helpers, reducers, domain functions): unit tests — many, fast, deterministic.
- Code with I/O (HTTP, DB, filesystem): integration tests behind a boundary mock (network-level or a test database), not by mocking internal functions.
- No real timers, no real network, no shared mutable fixtures. Wait for conditions, never sleep for fixed durations.
- Every bug fix ships with a test that fails before the fix and passes after.
- A flaky test is rewritten or deleted, never retried until green.
- Snapshot tests only for output that must not change byte-for-byte; never as a substitute for assertions.
- Test names state the behaviour ("rejects overlapping slots"), not the method name.
